5	/**
6	 * Single source of truth for an owner's {@code identityKey}: the one derived value that all
7	 * create-time duplicate detection for {@code POST /owners} is expressed through. It consolidates
8	 * what used to be three separate guards (telephone, email and household) into a single key, so a
9	 * request is a duplicate only when its <em>whole</em> key equals an existing owner's.
10	 *
11	 * <p>The key is {@code normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or
12	 * empty)}:
13	 * <ul>
14	 *   <li>telephone is canonicalised to E.164 ({@link OwnerTelephone#toE164(String)}) so the
15	 *       comparison is independent of how a value happens to be formatted;</li>
16	 *   <li>email is the stored lower-cased form ({@link OwnerEmail#normalize(String)}) when present,
17	 *       otherwise the empty string (email is optional);</li>
18	 *   <li>householdId is the owner's shared-household identifier when it carries one, otherwise the
19	 *       empty string.</li>
